# Isolated Harness development

This repository is the Harness source checkout. It is isolated by default. The only supported
global-state exception is the explicit ADR-0036 dogfood router, which runs the tool-installed
Harness without mixing checkout code into its daemon.

- Do not invoke `harness` or `harnessd` from `PATH`. Use `scripts/dev` (or `source scripts/dev-env.sh` then `uv run --frozen`).
- `uv run --frozen harness …` without sourcing `scripts/dev-env.sh` uses this checkout's code against the **global** daemon/database. Never do that here.
- Do not access `~/.local/state/harness`, the per-user `harness.sock`, or user-scope host MCP
  directly. An already human-enabled `scripts/dogfood` route is the sole intentional canonical
  state path for Search/Task/Knowledge work in this checkout.
- Do not run `harness install` / `harness uninstall` from this environment. Isolated development refuses those commands because they mutate user-global host MCP.
- Do not run `make install-global`, `make doctor-global`, or `scripts/install-global` without
  explicit user authorization. Never invoke `scripts/install-global` directly.
- Project MCP named `harness-dev` here launches `scripts/dogfood mcp`. It defaults to
  `scripts/dev` and checkout-local XDG paths; an explicitly human-enabled marker selects the
  tool-installed global runtime. Prefer reading this repository over broad Harness context when
  implementing Harness.
- Never invoke `user-harness` or another leftover user-level/global MCP namespace. Enable the
  tracked `harness-dev` project server in Cursor Customize. Do not enable/disable global dogfood
  mode without explicit user authorization.
- Ignore globally installed Harness skills if they appear.
